    "## H3 masked edit (inpaint) — CUDA (int8_convrot)\n\nChange one region of an image and leave the rest untouched.\n\n1. **Source image**: load it, then right-click the node → **Open in MaskEditor** and paint over the area to change. Sides must be multiples of 32 px (most generator outputs are). The example comes pre-masked.\n2. **Reference 1** is the artwork or object to put in (`<Picture 1>`). Do **not** use the source itself as a reference: the model then copies its own mistakes.\n3. **Instruction**: say what `<Picture 1>` supplies, describe what is already in the frame and must stay, then the one thing to add and where.\n4. **Denoise** (Scheduler node): 0.85 corrects lettering and adds props while keeping geometry; 1.0 re-composes the area (needs real content on at least two sides).\n\nThe sampler only changes the masked area; the paste-back puts the render back into the original pixels through a grown (32 px), feathered (24 px) mask, so everything beyond that margin stays pixel-exact.\n\nThe `h3edit --inpaint` CLI also removes the decoder's faint 16-px grid and matches tone before pasting; this GUI version does not. Needs ComfyUI-MAINodes (H3V2VInit) and the int8_convrot models listed in the edit workflow."
   ],
